WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.254
Idea. Imagine walking towards a wall, each step half as long as the last. Eight metres, four, two, one. You get closer and closer, but never pass a fixed distance.

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:24.191
If adding more terms gets closer and closer to a fixed number, the series is convergent. That number is the sum to infinity. If the total keeps growing, the series is not convergent.

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:39.179
For a geometric series it depends on the common ratio, r. If the size of r is less than one, the terms shrink. The size of r, written with two bars, is called the modulus. It means r without its sign.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:51.575
Four examples. A half shrinks. Minus a half swings up and down but shrinks. Three grows. Minus two swings and grows. The sign does not matter. Only the size does.

00:00:52.160 --> 00:01:02.943
These questions ask you to show a series is convergent, or explain why it has no sum to infinity. Find r, compare its size with one, and write a sentence.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:13.025
Method. Step one: find r. Divide the second term by the first. Check by dividing the third by the second. They must agree.

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:23.017
Step two: find the size of r and compare it with one. If it is less than one, the series is convergent. If it is one or more, it is not.

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:30.052
Step three: write a sentence with your value of r, how its size compares with one, and your conclusion.

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:48.305
Worked example. November twenty twenty, paper two. The first three terms are x minus three, x plus one, and four x minus two. From part a, x is one third or five. Given x is less than one, show the series is convergent. Two marks.

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:56.849
Step one: x is less than one, so x is one third. The terms are minus eight thirds, four thirds, minus two thirds.

00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:07.649
Step two: find r. Second over first is four thirds over minus eight thirds, which is minus a half. Third over second is also minus a half.

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:15.189
Step three: compare. The size of r is one half, which is less than one. So the series is convergent.

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:26.899
Reject a tempting route. Using x equal to five gives terms two, six, eighteen, so r is three. That is not convergent. This is why x is less than one.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:40.598
So the exam answer is: r is minus a half, so the size of r is less than one, so the series is convergent. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:54.185
Common mistake. A common mistake is to say r is less than one. Minus two is less than one, but a series with ratio minus two is not convergent. Use the size of r.

00:02:55.320 --> 00:03:11.382
Your turn. Now you try, from November twenty twenty five. A geometric series G has first term three plus root three. The second term is root three. Explain why G is convergent. Write your answer, then choose Continue to Answer.

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:29.705
Answer. First find r. Divide the second term by the first: root three over three plus root three. Multiply top and bottom by three minus root three. The bottom is nine minus three, which is six. So r is root three minus one, over two.

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:41.317
Root three is about one point seven three. So r is about nought point three seven. The exam answer: the size of r is less than one, so G is convergent.

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:55.915
The common wrong answer divides the wrong way: first term over second. That gives root three plus one, about two point seven three, so it says G is not convergent. Always divide a term by the one before it.

00:03:56.480 --> 00:04:02.053
Remember the method. Find r, find its size, compare with one, and write the sentence.
